# laptop — laptop power management + ergonomics pack (#25, PROPOSAL §14).
# Installed ONLINE on demand (official repos via pacman) — nothing baked or
# stashed (design pivot #42); only this name-list rides in the image as TEXT.
#
# POWER TOOLS ARE MUTUALLY EXCLUSIVE. power-profiles-daemon (the default),
# tlp, and auto-cpufreq each own the CPU-frequency/power policy and fight if
# co-installed. The #meta:conflicts line declares the two NON-DEFAULT tools
# (tlp, auto-cpufreq): the engine's ii_conflicts_check gate REFUSES the pack
# install BEFORE any pacman transaction if a foreign power tool is already
# present, so there is no half-applied state. (ppd is intentionally NOT in the
# manifest conflicts — it is a member here and the boxed-in system default, so a
# system already running ppd must NOT be refused.) The post-add hook then
# honours `--power=<ppd|tlp|auto-cpufreq>` (default ppd) and re-runs
# ii_conflicts_check on the OTHER two relative to the chosen tool before pacman,
# installs exactly the chosen tool, and enables exactly its one service via
# ii_service_enable (recorded; reversed on remove). tlp and auto-cpufreq are
# therefore NOT plain members — they are installed by the hook on demand.
#
# power-profiles-daemon ships as a plain member (the default), enabled by
# post-add. fprintd is the one unconditional member (brightnessctl is already
# baked via upstream's illogical-impulse-backlight dependency, so it is NOT
# re-declared here — listing an already-baked package would be a double-bake the
# validity lint forbids). fprintd is wired into login via an ii-OWNED PAM drop-in
# written by post-add (an additive file, never an in-place edit of a vendor
# /etc/pam.d/* file) and removed on post-remove. post-add also writes the
# sentinel-fenced power-widget launch line into ~/.config/hypr/custom/execs.lua
# (the widget QML is framework work, out of scope); post-remove strips it.
#meta:type laptop
#meta:conflicts tlp auto-cpufreq
power-profiles-daemon
fprintd
# Alternate power tools — installed by post-add only when selected via --power=;
# declared in #meta:conflicts above so the engine enforces the mutual exclusion:
#   tlp
#   auto-cpufreq
